# Third-party components

Core is free software under **LGPL-3.0-or-later** (`LICENSE`); the
documentation is **CC BY-SA 4.0** (`LICENSES/CC-BY-SA-4.0.txt`). This file lists
the third-party components and their licences; the full texts ship in
`LICENSES/`.

## Linked into a built product

| Component | Licence |
|---|---|
| Avalonia, Avalonia.Desktop, Avalonia.Fonts.Inter, Avalonia.Headless, Avalonia.Themes.Fluent, Avalonia.Wayland | MIT |
| The Inter font, embedded by `Avalonia.Fonts.Inter` | SIL Open Font License 1.1 |
| SkiaSharp and SkiaSharp.NativeAssets.* | MIT; the native Skia library is BSD-3-Clause |
| HarfBuzzSharp and HarfBuzzSharp.NativeAssets.* | MIT; the native HarfBuzz library is MIT |
| Tmds.DBus.Protocol | MIT |
| NWayland | MIT |
| MicroCom.Runtime | MIT |
| Avalonia.Angle.Windows.Natives (win-x64 only) | BSD-3-Clause |
| The .NET runtime libraries | MIT |

The native Skia/HarfBuzz packages ship their own `THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.txt`;
a product that redistributes the native assets must ship that notice too.
The copyright notices of the MIT-licensed components are those of their
upstream projects and ship in each package's `LICENSE`; the MIT text itself is
`LICENSES/MIT.txt`.

